# 64-bit build (milestone 12, way A): the CRI middleware (Sofdec movies, ADX
# sound) on LP64. Found with the tools in port/tools/m12 (view_check,
# decl_size_check, the -Wint-to-pointer-cast scan); on ILP32 nothing changes
# (every LP64 variant sits in #if __SIZEOF_POINTER__ != 4 or keeps the value).
# - Sint32/Uint32 stay 32 bits (exact_width_types in whole_prepare.py: the
#   game's own views of the CRI structures use int, mwply.h).
# - Addresses kept in Sint32 values (conditions SFSET_GetCond, ADXB x3c, the
#   SFD parameters ...) go back to pointers through Uint32: everything the
#   middleware handles lies at 0x80000000 and above, a signed value would
#   sign-extend (36 casts in src/lib; ARAM offsets and strides left alone).
# - mpv_lib.c: the default condition table holds the address of MPV_MbCbFn,
#   no 32-bit constant on LP64: MPV_Init stores it.
# - Size limits that are only sanity checks grow with the pointer size
#   (SFMPS_WORK_MAX); fixed tables the middleware defines as bytes get their
#   LP64 size with a check where the real type is visible (adx_fini.c ADXF
#   objects and command history, sfd_hds.c SFH work).
# - Partial views with the GameCube offsets in their pads (adx_bahx.c,
#   adx_bsc.c, adx_gc.c, adx_insh.c, mwsfdsl.c, sfx_sud.c): on LP64 the full
#   structure from its header (sfx.h names the user data pointer it hid).
# - The MPEG video handle (MPV_OBJ), viewed by five units under two names:
#   mpv.h's view names the pointers the other views keep in its pads (DCT
#   parameters, motion compensation work, frame planes); mpv_lib.c,
#   mpv_err.c, mpv_cmc.c and mpv_umc.c get LP64 views with explicit pads
#   generated from mpv.h's LP64 layout (all 177 GameCube offsets agree);
#   handle stride 0x1590 with size checks.
# - adx_tsvr.c / adx_sje.c: loops over per-channel members with a fixed
#   offset and a 4-byte step use the members on LP64.
# - Views of the Sofdec handle (SFD_OBJ) through a leading pad (sfd_buf.c,
#   sfd_pts.c, sfd_mps.c, sfd_mem.c) and of the player (mwsfdrna.c): LP64
#   pads generated from the full structure. The creation parameters' first
#   word is the driver table pointer (sfd.h, sfd_buf.c: as mwsfdcre.c types
#   it); the tag lookup in sfx_set.c passes SJCK chunks (pointer + length).
# - MPV_IXA, the table area mpv_bdec.c fills through an MPV_OBJ view, keeps
#   the tables at the LP64 MPV_OBJ offsets.
# - The concatenation work SFCON in SFD_OBJ is the timing work SFTIM_WORK
#   (sfd.h SFD_TIM): on LP64 sfd.h's SFCON is generated from SFTIM_WORK and
#   the pad behind it ends where SFTIM_WORK's members end (checked);
#   SFTIM_WORK's last word lies over the PTS queue pointer and is a pointer.
#   sfd_tim.c reads the clock source table through the GameCube offset 0xD28:
#   on LP64 the member timefn.
# - Video frame information: sfd.h's opaque SFD_VFRM_INF has the alignment of
#   sfd_mpv.c's SFMPV_VINF (8 on LP64, size checked), mwsfdfrm.c's view is
#   generated from it.
# - The three paired-single kernels of mpv_umc.c (asm translated by patch
#   0050) read the work and output block pointers at GameCube offsets: the
#   offsets come from the structures (the same values on ILP32, checked).
# - sfd_mem.c's view keeps the input buffer id (SFD_TR.bufout of driver 0) as
#   void *: on LP64 an id at its LP64 offset, as sfd_buf.c takes it.
# - sfd_mpv.c SFMPV_AddRead finds the frame slot 8 bytes before the frame
#   information it was handed: the offset of the member on LP64.
# - sfd_tim.c takes the frame information handed out by SFMPV_GetRead as an
#   SFD_VFRM (its slot) and reads the frame time through raw[3]/raw[4]: on
#   LP64 the words of SFMPV_VINF.ftime/tunit (checked in sfd_mpv.c).
